   "why_pair_coverage_is_not_the_success_statistic": "a pair lives in a space of N^2, so a pair birthday needs ~N visited pairs per trial against ~sqrt(2N) classes for a class birthday: at this budget the pair statistic is ~N^-1 of the class statistic, and it is not the event the pool replays.  Recovery needs two RECORDS in one class, produced at whatever steps each walker reached it; the invariant a + c*x == canon holds at every step of every walker, so x = (a1-a2)/(c2-c1) verifies with no shared future.  The pair number and the predecessor-matched fraction are reported so the reader can see the memory channel quantified; `success_raw` is the conversion measured end to end, and `merge` is the coverage statistic that the gate uses."
  },
  "passed": true,
  "rule": "CP-95 of the UNCONDITIONAL coverage (merge) rate >= 0.39 at the production-protocol densities d=5,7,9; the unconditional pool-detection rate success_raw is reported alongside and is not filtered by it",
  "unconditional": true,
  "why": "production success = P(two walkers occupy one class) minus the charged report lag 2*DP/S_ops = 2^-46; the toy's pool statistic needs records and its pool is budget/2^d per walker (1 at d=11, 2^46 in production), so it is the diagnostic, not the gate. d=11's walker has 0.18 DP spacings in its whole budget, i.e. it never restarts -- not the production protocol -- and it is reported in full"
